From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Settings > Accounts manages local accounts

The Accounts page managed Google accounts ("'s accounts", Add Google
Account, Family Link), which a NickelOS local account does not have and
which a de-Googled OS does not offer. For a local account it now shows the
nickel-accounts-card:
- Your account: name, picture, username, role, and Change password. The
  password is in two places, the encrypted home (cryptohome's
  local-password factor, what signing in checks) and the Linux user (sudo,
  polkit). The card checks the current password with cryptohome
  (quickUnlockPrivate.getAuthToken), changes the Linux one through
  nickel-accountsd (which checks the current password itself), then the
  encrypted home's (PasswordFactorEditor.updateOrSetLocalPassword); if that
  fails the Linux one is put back.
- Other people on this device (administrators): each account with its
  role, an Administrator toggle and Remove, both confirmed with the
  administrator's password (nickel-accountsd SetAdmin and RemoveUser; then
  ChromeOS removes the account and its encrypted home). The owner and the
  signed-in account are not removed; the last administrator stays one.
  Add person signs out, and the sign-in screen opens account creation
  (Local State nickel.add_person_at_sign_in).
NickelAccountsHandler (pages/people) talks to nickel-accountsd. Removing a
local account from the sign-in screen (its account menu) also removes the
Linux user now, once ChromeOS has removed the account, and its warning
no longer says the account "can still sign in later" (a Google account
can; a removed local account is gone with its files).

